BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE MADRAS HIGH COURT \(PRINCIPAL SEAT, CHENNAI\)
AT CHENNAI

CASE NO: CMA No. 2341 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: MHC010567892026
DECISION DATE: 2026-02-20
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice R. Subramanian

PARTIES:
United India Insurance Company Limited
... Appellant\(s\) / Petitioner\(s\)
Versus
Lakshmi and 3 others \(Legal heirs of deceased Rajan\)
... Respondent\(s\) / State

STATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:
Motor Vehicles Act 1988

SECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:
Motor Vehicles Act Section 166, Motor Vehicles Act Section 173

KEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:
Motor Accident Claims, Multiplier Method, Future Prospects, Loss of Dependency, Pranay Sethi

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTUAL MATRIX:
Tribunal awarded Rs. 42 Lakhs compensation adding 50% future prospects for a 46-year-old self-employed mason. Insurance company appealed on excessive quantum.

2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:
1. What is the appropriate addition for future prospects for a self-employed deceased aged between 40 and 50 years under National Insurance Co. Ltd. v. Pranay Sethi?

3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:
Constitution Bench in Pranay Sethi settled that where deceased was self-employed and aged 40-50, addition for future prospects must be 25%, not 50%.

4. RATIO DECIDENDI:
For self-employed victims aged between 40 and 50 years in motor accident claims, future prospects addition is legally capped at 25%.

5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:
Civil Miscellaneous Appeal Partly Allowed; Compensation recomputed from Rs. 42 Lakhs to Rs. 34.5 Lakhs following Pranay Sethi multiplier.

Decreed and ordered accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice R. Subramanian
Madras High Court \(Principal Seat, Chennai\)
